---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
---

<Base title="How It Works — MetaPainting">

  <Hero
    title="How It Works"
    subtitle="The MetaPainting method — from completed painting to masked surface to crowd collaboration."
    backgroundImage="/paintings/yoga-man/progress-3.jpg"
  />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container container--narrow">

      <div class="intro reveal">
        <p class="font-serif intro__text">
          MetaPainting is both a technique and a philosophy. Every piece begins as a finished painting
          by the artist. That painting is then masked, divided into numbered shapes, and opened to the
          crowd. Participants peel off a section, paint their contribution, and become inseparable from
          the work. The result is a layered collaboration — artist and community, structure and freedom,
          all woven together on one surface.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="principles reveal">
        <h3 class="font-display principles__title">Core Principles</h3>
        <div class="principles__grid">
          <div class="principle">
            <span class="principle__label font-display">Divide the Substrate</span>
            <p>Break the surface into distinct regions that give participants clear ownership of their area.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="principle">
            <span class="principle__label font-display">One Spot Only</span>
            <p>Each person paints one section. This creates genuine individual stakes in a collective outcome.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="principle">
            <span class="principle__label font-display">Respect Crowd as Medium</span>
            <p>The human is a separate layer with their own variables — prompt, mental state, time, skill, surroundings. Influence is a function.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="principle">
            <span class="principle__label font-display">Always Be Learning</span>
            <p>Every painting teaches something new. The method evolves with each piece.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="divider"></div>

      <!-- STEPS -->
      <div class="steps">

        <div class="step reveal">
          <div class="step__marker">
            <span class="step__number font-display">01</span>
          </div>
          <div class="step__content">
            <h3 class="step__title font-display">Design & Concept</h3>
            <p>Start with a theme, image, or idea. The design determines the outer shape, the internal
            divisions, and the palette. Consider how the crowd will interact with it — the size of
            individual shapes, what colors to allow, what constraints to set. A MetaPainting can be
            a shape, a logo, a theme, an icon, or a message.</p>
            <div class="step__tip">
              <strong>Layers and Dials:</strong> Think about the elements of art — color, form, line,
              shape, space, texture, value — and how to distribute them consciously across layers.
              Variables like shape size, allowed colors, instruments, time constraints, and prompts
              are "dials" you can tune for each painting.
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="step reveal">
          <div class="step__marker">
            <span class="step__number font-display">02</span>
          </div>
          <div class="step__content">
            <h3 class="step__title font-display">The Painting (Underpainting)</h3>
            <p>This is a complete, finished work of art. Not a sketch or an outline — a real painting
            that could stand on its own. Acrylic on wood is the most common substrate. The underpainting
            establishes the foundation that the collaborative layer will interact with. This is the
            artist's vision, rendered in full before anyone else touches it.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="step reveal">
          <div class="step__marker">
            <span class="step__number font-display">03</span>
          </div>
          <div class="step__content">
            <h3 class="step__title font-display">The Masking</h3>
            <p>Once the painting is complete, the entire surface is covered with a masking layer.
            That layer is then divided into shapes — numbered or lettered — and finely cut so each
            section can be peeled off individually. This is precise, painstaking work. The mask
            pattern determines how the crowd will experience the painting: the size and distribution
            of shapes, whether they follow the image or cut across it, how many participants the
            painting can accommodate.</p>
            <div class="step__tip">
              <strong>SpaceTape</strong> is a key material — it creates clean divisions between
              sections while protecting the underpainting beneath.
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="step reveal">
          <div class="step__marker">
            <span class="step__number font-display">04</span>
          </div>
          <div class="step__content">
            <h3 class="step__title font-display">The Collaboration</h3>
            <p>This is where it happens. Participants pick a numbered or lettered spot, peel off the
            mask for that section, and paint directly onto the surface. They're painting on top of and
            into the underpainting — their contribution becomes permanently layered with the artist's
            original work. Think jams and exquisite corpse — controlled chaos within a framework.</p>
            <div class="step__tip">
              <strong>Crowd flow:</strong> At a festival, expect 10-30 participants per day. At a
              4-hour event, 5-7 is typical. Manage palettes, wash brushes, explain the constraints,
              and keep the energy moving. The surrounding art evolves as each person contributes,
              which changes the experience for the next participant.
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="step reveal">
          <div class="step__marker">
            <span class="step__number font-display">05</span>
          </div>
          <div class="step__content">
            <h3 class="step__title font-display">Completion & Refinement</h3>
            <p>Once all sections are painted, the piece enters a refinement phase. This may include
            filling gaps, applying a light corrective hand, adding finishing layers, or — in some
            paintings — applying phosphorescent or UV-reactive paint for a blacklight reveal.
            Not every painting uses these effects; they're one tool among many.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="step reveal">
          <div class="step__marker">
            <span class="step__number font-display">06</span>
          </div>
          <div class="step__content">
            <h3 class="step__title font-display">Protect the Painting</h3>
            <p>The work is a living record of a shared moment. Seal it, document it, and present
            it. Every MetaPainting carries the story of its creation — the participants, the event,
            the energy in the room. That story is as much a part of the art as the paint on the surface.</p>
            <div class="step__tip">
              <strong>A word on protection:</strong> Always be ready to protect the painting from
              accidents and bad actors. It has happened. The work of dozens of collaborators
              deserves to be defended.
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>

      <!-- CTA -->
      <div class="hiw-cta reveal">
        <h3 class="font-display hiw-cta__title">Ready to Try It Yourself?</h3>
        <p class="hiw-cta__desc">
          Download vector templates and masking guides to get started, or commission a guided MetaPainting experience.
        </p>
        <div class="hiw-cta__actions">
          <a href="/templates" class="btn btn--primary">Get Templates</a>
          <a href="/commission" class="btn btn--outline">Commission a Painting</a>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

</Base>

<style>
  .intro {
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
  }

  .intro__text {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.8;
    max-width: 700px;
  }

  .principles {
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
  }

  .principles__title {
    font-size: 2rem;
    color: var(--color-text);
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.03em;
  }

  .principles__grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }

  .principle {
    padding: 1.25rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
  }

  .principle__label {
    display: block;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    color: var(--color-teal);
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.03em;
  }

  .principle p {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .steps {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 3.5rem;
    padding-top: 2rem;
  }

  .step {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 60px 1fr;
    gap: 2rem;
  }

  .step__marker {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
  }

  .step__number {
    font-size: 1.4rem;
    color: var(--color-teal);
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
  }

  .step__title {
    font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 3vw, 2.2rem);
    color: var(--color-text);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.03em;
  }

  .step__content p {
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.75;
    max-width: 650px;
  }

  .step__tip {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
    background: var(--color-surface-2);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--color-teal);
    border-radius: 0 var(--radius) var(--radius) 0;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .step__tip strong {
    color: var(--color-teal);
  }

  .hiw-cta {
    text-align: center;
    padding: 4rem 0 2rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    margin-top: 4rem;
  }

  .hiw-cta__title {
    font-size: 2.5rem;
    color: var(--color-text);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
  }

  .hiw-cta__desc {
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .hiw-cta__actions {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1rem;
    justify-content: center;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .step {
      grid-template-columns: 40px 1fr;
      gap: 1rem;
    }

    .principles__grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
